  "rules": [
    "Clinical study objective precedes observations and summaries.",
    "Probability cases combine validity, full CDF, sketches, moments and boundary probabilities.",
    "Inference cases require method choice, population null, calculation, table decision and contextual conclusion.",
    "Differentiate all-pairs and against-control families; retain ANOVA residual variance and df.",
    "Use original unrounded counts for pooling; apply course Yates convention to 2x2.",
    "Balanced ANOVA only; no manual sums-of-squares, Session 14 or code-writing tasks."
  ],
  "interpretation": "Scores prioritize preparation using explicit review and assignment evidence. Feature counts describe actual source task language; they are not fitted probabilities for unseen exam questions."
